The failed judgement is AC-1's `when` step "square six" (score {"halve": 1}, threshold 9). The step is of the right kind (an action), but it names squaring. The product description states: "The calculator offers one operation, Halve, which displays half the entered number. It has no Square operation." Every other part of the Story already says halving — title "Halve a number", i_want "to halve a number", so_that "I can read its half", AC-1 description "The number must be halved", and the then step "three is displayed" (three is half of six, not the square of six). The `when` step is therefore a wording slip in the Item, not a gap in the concept set.

No wider concept and no new concept is warranted:
- A new variation would widen "halve" to cover squaring, which contradicts the product description (no Square operation).
- A new `when` concept for squaring would introduce an operation the product does not offer.
So the smallest correct repair is to restate the step as the halve action the rest of the Story already asserts.

